WEBVTT

00:06.487 --> 00:07.707
Hey! Listen!

00:08.307 --> 00:10.667
Don't you want to get that book back?

00:18.047 --> 00:19.007
Huh?

00:28.907 --> 00:31.597
<b>Jaadugar</b>

01:51.407 --> 01:56.407
<b>An Enduring Flame</b>

01:51.827 --> 01:56.857
<i>The 13th century saw the rise 
of a vast empire across Eurasia.</i>

01:57.397 --> 02:00.027
<i>Genghis Khan, the "universal ruler."</i>

02:01.007 --> 02:06.447
<i>Hailed as the Great Khan, he and his kin
 built the Mongol Empire.</i>

02:07.387 --> 02:10.677
<i>Although the Mongols 
were originally but a tiny tribe,</i>

02:10.677 --> 02:17.407
<i>by A.D. 1206, they had conquered the other
steppe tribes and become a major power.</i>

02:17.407 --> 02:24.257
<i>Not long after, they forayed into 
the various nations bordering the steppe.</i>

02:22.647 --> 02:26.317
<b>Spring, A.D. 1221
Taloqan</b>

02:28.177 --> 02:30.467
<b>Fourth Prince
Tolui</b>

02:28.657 --> 02:30.467
Greetings, brothers.

02:30.467 --> 02:31.717
Tolui.

02:32.927 --> 02:34.987
<b>Third Prince
Ögedei</b>

02:35.407 --> 02:37.407
<b>Second Prince
Chagatai</b>

02:35.607 --> 02:37.057
Haven't you drunk enough?

02:38.017 --> 02:39.267
Welcome back.

02:38.197 --> 02:40.157
<b>First Prince
Jochi</b>

02:43.467 --> 02:45.357
How did the campaign in Khwarazm go?

02:46.837 --> 02:48.817
Favorably, except...

02:49.127 --> 02:51.187
We lost a lot of soldiers.

02:51.447 --> 02:52.347
The shame is mine.

02:52.347 --> 02:54.227
Your indecision is to blame, Jochi.

02:54.227 --> 02:56.717
All you had to do 
was follow Father's orders.

02:56.717 --> 02:58.377
That's enough, you two.

02:59.067 --> 03:02.087
What about you, Tolui? 
You were in Persia, I believe?

03:03.107 --> 03:03.707
Indeed.

03:03.707 --> 03:06.847
I did the name of
Genghis Khan proud in battle.

03:07.447 --> 03:10.977
As befits the Otchigin, 
our future emperor.

03:18.337 --> 03:21.267
Not to mention, I acquired something good.

03:24.177 --> 03:25.537
A book in a foreign tongue?

03:25.537 --> 03:27.737
I hear it's called <i>Elements</i>.

03:28.737 --> 03:33.697
My wife asked me for this book 
as a token of my exploits.

03:33.697 --> 03:36.467
What a modest woman she is!

03:36.467 --> 03:39.237
She could have asked 
for gold or jewels instead.

03:40.757 --> 03:44.507
I would do anything to make her happy.

03:46.127 --> 03:47.757
So what's written in this book?

03:51.247 --> 03:52.347
No idea.

03:53.697 --> 03:57.127
Oh, so you have a scholar 
who can explain its contents?

03:57.127 --> 03:58.257
Nope.

03:58.257 --> 04:01.307
Can your wife read foreign tongues?

04:01.307 --> 04:02.927
I don't think so.

04:04.047 --> 04:05.227
Oh dear.

04:08.097 --> 04:12.407
As such, I was hoping 
to introduce you to Prince Tolui.

04:12.957 --> 04:14.947
You're a scholar's daughter, no?

04:15.287 --> 04:17.707
I'd have preferred 
to volunteer myself instead,

04:17.707 --> 04:20.247
but sadly, I can only read 
and write simple things.

04:20.957 --> 04:23.487
I do pick up
 new languages quickly, though.

04:24.827 --> 04:27.837
Why did she want the book?

04:27.837 --> 04:30.147
Huh? No clue.

04:30.147 --> 04:31.797
She can't even read what's in it.

04:31.797 --> 04:34.597
And she asked for it 
instead of gold or silver.

04:34.597 --> 04:36.267
An odd request, to be sure.

04:36.727 --> 04:40.007
Still, this is your chance 
to serve the imperial family.

04:40.007 --> 04:42.437
And to have that book in your hands again.

04:42.747 --> 04:45.207
Not a bad deal, wouldn't you say?

04:47.167 --> 04:51.527
<i>The Mongol emperor? Serve his family?</i>

04:51.917 --> 04:54.907
<i>No, before that... Before all of that...</i>

04:55.347 --> 04:58.617
<i>My wife asked me for this book.</i>

05:01.787 --> 05:04.927
<i>My mistress died for that?!</i>

05:06.947 --> 05:11.427
Um, what happened to your family
 was, uh, unfortunate.

05:11.427 --> 05:13.587
So let me apologize.

05:13.587 --> 05:16.097
But I didn't have a choice.

05:16.347 --> 05:19.817
I'm doing all I can 
to get in their good favor.

05:19.817 --> 05:21.977
I don't want to be sent
 to the front lines.

05:22.517 --> 05:26.857
Boys my age end up at the very front
 of their expedition armies.

05:27.237 --> 05:28.727
To act as human shields.

05:31.447 --> 05:36.187
You're not old enough to grow a beard. 
They took you captive?

05:36.187 --> 05:37.227
That's right.

05:37.707 --> 05:40.037
No, enough talking about the past.

05:40.037 --> 05:42.247
This is my chance to move up in the world.

05:42.247 --> 05:43.727
With this new social order,

05:43.727 --> 05:46.997
a path to success based on merit
 has opened up to us.

05:46.997 --> 05:49.627
I'll do whatever it takes 
to survive and make it big.

05:49.627 --> 05:52.717
Now's your chance to make 
the most of your education.

05:52.717 --> 05:54.927
And that fetching face of yours.

05:55.267 --> 05:59.887
If the stars align, you could become 
an attendant to a high-ranking figure.

06:01.567 --> 06:04.377
As you can see, 
her smile is quite fetching.

06:05.787 --> 06:08.547
That's why you should do something.

06:08.547 --> 06:10.227
But what, exactly?

06:10.837 --> 06:15.077
<i>How could I possibly know 
what course of action to take here?</i>

06:16.517 --> 06:18.117
<i>What should I do?</i>

06:22.107 --> 06:23.907
But if you study and become wise,

06:23.907 --> 06:29.017
you will know the best course of action
 to take, whatever trouble you're in.

06:42.867 --> 06:47.347
I am well-versed in ancient wisdom 
and modern teachings alike.

06:47.767 --> 06:49.217
It goes without saying...

06:49.687 --> 06:51.977
that I can read that book, 
Euclid's <i>Elements</i>.

06:54.007 --> 06:55.217
You're right.

06:57.377 --> 07:01.047
I want to lead a cushy life,
eating good food every day.

07:04.707 --> 07:06.847
This might just be my big chance!

07:06.847 --> 07:09.857
I'm sure we can make it happen 
if we work together!

07:09.857 --> 07:11.627
Y-Yeah.

07:12.167 --> 07:15.847
M-My name is Shira. I hail from Samarkand.

07:17.167 --> 07:18.897
I'm Sitara.

07:18.897 --> 07:19.987
Sitara?

07:20.417 --> 07:21.567
Uh, hold on.

07:21.567 --> 07:23.277
An ostentatious name like that...

07:23.277 --> 07:26.247
Yes, I'm a slave. What of it?

07:28.587 --> 07:30.447
It may be a new social order,

07:30.447 --> 07:33.107
but being wellborn
 still gets you a long way.

07:33.487 --> 07:36.267
Especially when dealing 
with the imperial family.

07:37.107 --> 07:39.067
Well, I guess you can just lie.

07:39.487 --> 07:41.447
Let's go with a more dignified name.

07:43.307 --> 07:44.537
In that case...

07:46.177 --> 07:47.177
<i>Tumen commander.</i>

07:47.427 --> 07:50.927
<i>This is the young lady I spoke of.</i>

07:51.517 --> 07:53.267
<i>Oh, I'm her interpreter, Shira.</i>

07:53.637 --> 07:56.147
<i>Pleased to make your acquaintance.</i>

07:58.247 --> 07:59.177
Listen up.

07:59.177 --> 08:04.497
Anyone granted an audience with 
the Mongols must pass between two fires.

08:04.497 --> 08:07.487
They believe fire has 
the power to purify evil.

08:08.307 --> 08:10.187
A heathen ritual, huh?

08:17.357 --> 08:20.817
Also, <i>definitely</i> don't step 
on the entrance's threshold.

08:21.297 --> 08:23.197
If you do, you'll be put to death.

08:37.437 --> 08:39.147
<i>Greetings, scholar's daughter!</i>

08:40.107 --> 08:42.527
<i>Glad to see you're still alive.</i>

08:42.857 --> 08:47.977
<i>"Greetings, scholar's daughter! Glad to see
you're still alive," says His Highness.</i>

08:48.527 --> 08:52.067
"'Greetings, scholar's daughter! 
Glad to see you're still alive,'

08:52.067 --> 08:53.937
says His Highness," he says.

08:54.157 --> 08:56.577
<i>Yes, you seem much more obedient now.</i>

08:57.077 --> 08:57.707
<i>Commendable.</i>

08:59.877 --> 09:01.587
<i>Have you been told the details?</i>

09:02.127 --> 09:04.417
<i>I want you to wait on my wife
and explain that book to her.</i>

09:04.757 --> 09:06.217
<i>She'll surely be delighted.</i>

09:07.177 --> 09:08.507
<i>Oh, right. What's your name?</i>

09:10.277 --> 09:11.997
My name...

09:15.127 --> 09:18.087
is Fatima.

09:25.067 --> 09:27.697
<i>These fires will never be enough
 to erase them.</i>

09:30.437 --> 09:34.227
<i>Not those tender days that no longer exist
 outside of my memories.</i>

09:35.047 --> 09:37.507
<i>Nor my ties to the mistress
 and the others.</i>

09:39.757 --> 09:44.567
<i>If there's one thing I can still do, 
it's taking that book back.</i>

09:45.617 --> 09:49.577
<i>I shall remain my mistress's slave
 until that day.</i>

10:06.487 --> 10:11.217
I've avoided a fate on the front lines, 
thanks to the commander's good word.

10:11.607 --> 10:13.277
Is she Tolui's wife?

10:13.277 --> 10:18.687
No, Princess Sorghaghtani should be 
at the Mongols' home camp, way out east.

10:19.677 --> 10:22.987
Who could she be? 
One of the generals' wives?

10:22.987 --> 10:23.897
What?

10:23.897 --> 10:28.567
The Mongols always bring a number of women
with them, even on military expeditions.

10:28.567 --> 10:30.697
Women on an expedition?

10:30.697 --> 10:33.007
I can't even begin to imagine it.

10:35.037 --> 10:37.427
<i>First, I need to learn about them.</i>

10:38.597 --> 10:41.857
Shira, teach me some 
simple Mongolian words.

10:41.857 --> 10:43.527
I want to get ahead apace.

10:43.527 --> 10:46.717
Then, in return, I ask that 
you help me in times of need.

10:47.297 --> 10:48.567
Why, of course.

10:48.567 --> 10:50.607
We're on the same side, aren't we?

10:51.597 --> 10:55.637
<i>Everyone here is my enemy.</i>

10:57.267 --> 11:01.817
<i>I'll fight to the bitter end, 
as alone as I may be.</i>

11:13.917 --> 11:16.367
I searched all over for you, Töregene.

11:16.787 --> 11:18.037
Prince Ögedei.

11:20.787 --> 11:25.507
Dear me. Not a single word of appreciation 
for your husband returned from battle?

11:26.597 --> 11:30.047
I am not your wife.

11:30.527 --> 11:32.227
I'm your enemy.

11:41.587 --> 11:43.927
<i>The year is 1221.</i>

11:44.237 --> 11:48.227
<i>After a brief period of rest in Taloqan,
the Mongol army...</i>

11:49.297 --> 11:52.437
<i>sets out once more in the autumn.</i>

11:53.437 --> 11:56.957
<i>One of Central Asia's great powers:
the Khwarazmian Empire.</i>

11:57.627 --> 12:01.877
<i>The Mongols head south 
to vanquish its last ruler.</i>

12:02.687 --> 12:08.287
<i>This conflict would go down in history
as the Battle of the Indus.</i>

12:10.517 --> 12:12.847
<i>Meanwhile, unlit by 
the spotlight of history,</i>

12:12.847 --> 12:18.627
<i>those taken captive in Persia continued 
their long march to the Mongol home camp.</i>

12:19.237 --> 12:20.897
Half a year has passed.

12:20.897 --> 12:22.807
How much longer will it take?

12:22.807 --> 12:24.227
Halt!

12:27.117 --> 12:29.377
Begin constructing the tents at once!

12:29.377 --> 12:34.167
An honored guest of the Great Khan 
is heading this way from the east.

12:34.167 --> 12:37.327
We are to set up camp and provide him 
with lodging for the night.

12:44.887 --> 12:46.707
Help. I can.

12:47.637 --> 12:50.297
No, this is a job for a man.

12:55.807 --> 12:57.377
Understand.

12:59.407 --> 13:03.937
<i>There's still much about the Mongols'
 way of life that puzzles me.</i>

13:04.447 --> 13:07.107
<i>But slowly, I'm growing to understand it.</i>

13:09.437 --> 13:12.157
They're all hopeless without me.

13:12.157 --> 13:16.847
<i>For example, the entrances of their tents
 always face southwards.</i>

13:16.847 --> 13:19.327
You there! It's time to give water
 to the livestock!

13:19.327 --> 13:23.537
<i>What's more, they follow 
a rigorous daily schedule.</i>

13:26.797 --> 13:30.847
<i>I wonder how they keep track of the time.</i>

13:37.987 --> 13:40.467
<i>I see. It's a sundial.</i>

13:40.837 --> 13:44.227
<i>Where the light falls inside the house
 tells them the time.</i>

13:46.127 --> 13:49.297
<i>That's pretty clever, 
having the whole house act as a clock.</i>

13:50.847 --> 13:54.727
<i>An astrolabe would tell the time
 more precisely, though.</i>

13:54.727 --> 13:56.757
<i>This is nothing but the wisdom of savages.</i>

14:06.287 --> 14:07.437
Have you heard?

14:07.437 --> 14:11.967
Tonight's guest is an eastern sage who 
knows the secret to immortality, they say.

14:11.967 --> 14:13.247
Immortality?

14:13.247 --> 14:14.887
Excuse me.

14:14.887 --> 14:18.867
We are Uyghurs from the city nearby.

14:18.867 --> 14:21.707
We come with an offering 
for the master sage.

14:21.707 --> 14:23.437
Could you show us to him?

14:23.437 --> 14:24.147
What?

14:24.147 --> 14:25.767
No, I'm too scared.

14:25.767 --> 14:26.807
But...

14:27.047 --> 14:31.387
<i>I admit the idea of an immortal
 is rather creepy. Even so...</i>

14:34.237 --> 14:35.947
This way.

14:36.827 --> 14:38.407
Is that you, chieftain?

14:38.407 --> 14:40.087
Oh, Chinqai!

14:40.087 --> 14:42.707
You were accompanying the sage?

14:42.707 --> 14:46.457
Oh, pardon me. 
I meant to call you Lord Chinqai.

14:46.457 --> 14:50.207
No need for that. You helped me out
 greatly when I was a mere peddler.

14:50.747 --> 14:52.437
For the master sage.

14:52.437 --> 14:56.427
Wine, bread, and watermelon 
from our city of Janbaliq.

14:56.427 --> 14:58.137
W-Watermelon!

14:58.607 --> 15:01.347
These look wonderful. Please head inside.

15:02.177 --> 15:04.047
Here. You bring this.

15:04.047 --> 15:04.807
Huh?

15:05.397 --> 15:07.767
U-Um, I'm not...

15:08.637 --> 15:10.607
What's the matter? Follow them.

15:10.607 --> 15:11.727
But...

15:14.367 --> 15:16.197
<i>An immortal?</i>

15:16.877 --> 15:18.917
<i>Someone like that can't </i>really<i> exist.</i>

15:18.917 --> 15:21.157
<i>I'll go see the truth for myself.</i>

15:26.707 --> 15:28.207
Allow me to introduce him.

15:28.207 --> 15:34.967
Invited by the Great Khan, 
and currently making his way westward:

15:34.967 --> 15:38.837
the sage, Master Changchun.

15:38.837 --> 15:41.097
<i>Has he been alive for 200 years?</i>

15:41.097 --> 15:43.207
<i>I'm terrified!</i>

15:43.207 --> 15:44.937
The offering, if you will.

15:55.437 --> 15:57.897
Master Changchun asks the following.

15:58.417 --> 16:02.367
"Did anyone here see the solar eclipse 
on the first day of the fifth month?"

16:03.597 --> 16:05.377
The solar eclipse?

16:05.377 --> 16:07.077
Oh, yes, there was one, indeed.

16:07.387 --> 16:09.037
During the hour of the snake.

16:09.387 --> 16:12.747
About 7/10ths of the sun 
must have been obscured.

16:12.967 --> 16:14.837
I-I, too.

16:15.377 --> 16:17.187
I also saw.

16:17.937 --> 16:23.507
That day, passing near Samarkand.

16:23.967 --> 16:30.477
Sky grew slightly dark.
 Sun, about 6/10ths, blocked.

16:33.237 --> 16:35.107
<i>Crescent shadows through the trees.</i>

16:36.267 --> 16:37.687
<i>A solar eclipse.</i>

16:38.817 --> 16:42.067
<i>Master Muhammad might've kept
 a record of this.</i>

16:42.067 --> 16:44.757
<i>But I don't even know 
the exact time right now.</i>

16:48.477 --> 16:51.327
That time. Light from the sun.

16:52.227 --> 16:56.757
Shone on edge of roof poles. In tent.

16:57.997 --> 17:00.347
The edge of the roof poles 
signals the hour of the dragon.

17:00.347 --> 17:04.217
In other words, the eclipse 
started later around here?

17:04.217 --> 17:09.287
Master Changchun saw the eclipse 
at the Kherlen River to the east.

17:09.287 --> 17:10.447
The time was midday.

17:10.447 --> 17:11.937
So even later.

17:13.647 --> 17:16.277
He was able to see the stars in the sky.

17:17.617 --> 17:20.317
There are different degrees 
of eclipsing as well?

17:22.927 --> 17:27.297
"During a solar eclipse, 
the moon casts its shadow over the sun."

17:27.297 --> 17:32.077
"One could liken it to obstructing
 this flame with a fan."

17:32.717 --> 17:35.067
"From where I sit, 
the flame is not visible,

17:35.067 --> 17:37.497
but the rest of you 
see a different picture."

17:39.397 --> 17:42.597
The world is a wide place, indeed.

17:44.927 --> 17:48.927
I'm sorry I didn't realize 
you weren't with them.

17:49.677 --> 17:52.797
I'm Chinqai, an Uyghur.

17:52.797 --> 17:56.147
I learned a bit of Persian 
in my peddling days.

17:57.127 --> 18:00.157
M-My name is Fatima.

18:00.157 --> 18:04.277
I'm traveling east so I may serve 
the consort of Prince Tolui.

18:04.277 --> 18:06.947
Oh, Tolui's wife, Princess Sorghaghtani?

18:08.027 --> 18:10.297
So you're her lady-in-waiting, huh?

18:10.297 --> 18:12.997
The cleverness you displayed
 makes sense now.

18:13.447 --> 18:15.167
You're too kind.

18:15.797 --> 18:17.627
And well, um...

18:18.007 --> 18:22.217
May I be so bold as to ask, um, 
how old the master sage is?

18:24.557 --> 18:27.137
You wish to know more about immortality?

18:27.617 --> 18:33.047
Unfortunately, I can't reveal his secret 
to you before the Great Khan.

18:34.677 --> 18:38.307
No, I have no interest 
in becoming immortal.

18:38.687 --> 18:41.827
There was a story in a book I once read.

18:42.517 --> 18:46.527
It was about a man who traveled
to India in search of longevity.

18:46.527 --> 18:48.287
But the men he found there

18:48.287 --> 18:52.287
cared for their fathers and grandfathers
who were too elderly to even stand.

18:52.757 --> 18:54.177
Furthermore...

18:54.177 --> 18:55.707
My great-grandfather.

18:55.707 --> 18:59.167
I must cover him with this sheet, 
lest the rats nibble away at him.

18:59.567 --> 19:02.667
Even so, he's alive 
and blessed with longevity.

19:03.377 --> 19:07.217
Upon hearing this, the man 
no longer sought an extended life.

19:08.687 --> 19:11.857
Instead of attaining immortality
 by defying Allah,

19:11.857 --> 19:15.187
it's better to welcome a healthy 
and natural death.

19:15.187 --> 19:17.227
That was the moral of the tale.

19:18.837 --> 19:22.437
Actually, Master Changchun 
divulged it to me.

19:22.827 --> 19:24.897
The secret to immortality.

19:27.217 --> 19:31.777
You're a bright girl, so I'll make 
an exception and share it with you.

19:32.007 --> 19:35.117
The secret to immortality is...

19:37.777 --> 19:38.977
...nonexistent.

19:38.977 --> 19:41.657
We must all welcome a healthy 
and natural death.

19:45.347 --> 19:47.907
I see sages can be found 
to the east and west alike.

19:48.977 --> 19:52.977
Our empire may be mighty, 
but it's also still young.

19:52.977 --> 19:55.427
There are many things 
we have yet to learn.

19:55.667 --> 20:00.287
Fatima, your wisdom is something
we need greatly.

20:11.657 --> 20:15.407
A path to success based on merit 
has opened up to us.

20:16.507 --> 20:19.867
<i>What exactly can I do?</i>

20:20.717 --> 20:23.797
I... intend to go on a journey.

20:25.137 --> 20:27.047
<i>Back then...</i>

20:28.947 --> 20:31.737
<i>Why did I feel such frustration?</i>

20:36.447 --> 20:39.807
<b>Several Months Later</b>

20:39.807 --> 20:41.727
Keep walking! We're almost there!

20:48.007 --> 20:49.607
We have returned.

20:58.947 --> 21:02.737
<i>According to the map of the world 
by al-Biruni I once saw...</i>

21:03.847 --> 21:06.727
<i>I now find myself at its very edge.</i>

21:14.097 --> 21:15.047
So cold!

21:15.347 --> 21:17.117
I-I can't believe how cold it is!

21:17.117 --> 21:18.817
I'm freezing!

21:18.817 --> 21:20.167
Put these on.

21:20.687 --> 21:23.267
Welcome to Princess Sorghaghtani's orda.

21:23.267 --> 21:27.567
Her Highness has prepared coats 
and warm tents for you.

21:35.757 --> 21:37.737
Is there a girl named Fatima here?

21:43.497 --> 21:46.457
Princess Sorghaghtani, I've brought her.

21:53.167 --> 21:57.347
<b>First Wife of Tolui
Sorghaghtani Beki</b>

21:53.167 --> 21:57.347
Thank you for making 
the long journey here in this cold.

22:00.977 --> 22:04.597
You're the one who will be 
teaching me this book, yes?

